= How to use this book

Read the chapter objectives and sections before attempting the worked examples. Answer the two-minute set and the 40-question drill without looking at the key. Mark every item, read the explanation and record why any error occurred.

The timed papers provide mixed practice under a time limit. Use the rapid-fire section and glossary for retrieval, the model answers to strengthen explanations, and the comparison and trap tables to distinguish similar concepts.

This volume covers movement, the body, fitness, sport and inclusive participation. Volume 2 is planned to cover personal and community health. This editorial division does not imply separate JAMB examinations. The topic plan uses a secondary outline and has not been independently verified against the current official JAMB syllabus. Check that syllabus and the subject requirements of your chosen programme and institution. This book is not a substitute for individual medical advice.

== A practical study cycle

+ *Learn:* explain a diagram or key distinction in your own words.
+ *Apply:* work through the examples and explain the reasoning.
+ *Test:* complete the drill before checking the key; record uncertain items.
+ *Review:* identify knowledge, interpretation or calculation errors and revisit the section.
+ *Revisit:* try a different question after a gap and explain your answer.

#rule-box("Before taking a timed paper")[
  Use a clock and attempt the full set in one sitting. After marking, read explanations for correct answers as well as mistakes; a correct guess does not establish understanding. Questions are original practice, not purported past JAMB questions.
]

The master bank contains fifteen questions per chapter. Take care with individual differences, safety and the rules specified in each question.
